      <CaveatCard title="What these numbers are">
        <ul class="list-disc pl-4 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Synthetic benchmark values, not live multi-turn chat speed.</li>
          <li>Author-measured: two phones, two models, one quantization pair. Not a universal multiplier - the contributed dataset exists to widen exactly this.</li>
          <li>Single-run rows are indicative only; the observed single-pass noise floor is roughly ±15-20%.</li>
          <li>Power and tok/W are recorded only while unplugged; the app hides them while charging because USB input invalidates the battery-current reading.</li>
        </ul>
      </CaveatCard>
      <CaveatCard title="Evidence status">
        <p>
          The per-pass CSVs for the v2.0.0 reference runs were never retained - the export was
          broken (Android killed the activity behind the file picker and every export produced a
          0-byte CSV plus a "CSV exported" toast; fixed in v2.1.0 by staging to cache). Since
          then seven raw exports are retained in <code>benchmarks/results/</code>, including
          both five-run four-arm records and the contributed-dataset CSV. Competitor figures are
          read off each app's own results screen - reproducible by installing the same apps, but
          not re-analysable; ENTITY's own figure comes from ENTITY Bench, whose per-run CSV is
          the only raw evidence any of the three apps can produce.
